## Room for a million connections: one Erlang process and one port (socket) per connection, plus the pools.
+P 4194304
+Q 2097152

## Every garbage collection is a full sweep, so the heaps of a million mostly idle processes shrink back to
## what they hold instead of keeping the size they grew to while serving a request.
-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 0

## UTF-8 file names even without a UTF-8 locale (as under systemd)
+fnu

## Schedulers sleep when idle instead of spinning: the kernel's network processing runs on these cores too.
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
